       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Jared Whiklo",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4c12a753d0071341edb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p><a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=6089a135248ef6007394556d\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"6089a135248ef6007394556d\" data-account-id=\"6089a135248ef6007394556d\" accountid=\"6089a135248ef6007394556d\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Former user</a> this is working correctly because you are attempting to delete objects with unbound variables.</p>\n\n<p>You need do perform something like this</p>\n<div class=\"preformatted panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"preformattedContent panelContent\">\n<pre>DELETE {\r\n  &lt;&gt; dc:title ?o1 ;\r\n     dc:author ?o2 .\r\n}\r\nWHERE {\r\n  &lt;&gt; dc:title ?o1 .\r\n  OPTIONAL {\r\n     &lt;&gt; dc:author ?o2 .\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n</pre>\n</div></div>\n\n<p>However if the target resource does not have a <tt>dc:title</tt> property the entire SPARQL update will not match and will not update any properties.</p>\n\n<p>Might be better to send each DELETE as a separate SPARQL update inside a transaction.</p>",
